hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7756","7802 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of Iyad bin Himar Al-Mujashi’i, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty has commanded me to teach you what You are ignorant of what this day of mine has taught me. He said to me: Everything that I made lawful for My servants is lawful for them. And I created My servants, all of them pure. Then the devils came to them and induced them to abandon their religion, and I prohibited for them what I had made lawful for them, and I commanded them to associate with Me that which I had not revealed. authority, and indeed God Almighty looked at the people of the earth and abhorred them, their Arabs and non-Arabs, except for remnants of the People of the Book, and indeed God God Almighty commanded me to burn the Quraysh, so I said: O Lord, they are making my head so heavy that they call it bread. He said: I have only sent you to test you. And He has afflicted you, and I have sent down to you a book that cannot be washed away by water, which you read in your dreams and while awake, so fight them and we will fight you, and spend. It will be spent on you, and send an army, and we will supply you with five times their number, and fight with those who obey you and those who disobey you. Then he said: The people of Paradise are three: an imam. He is just, a merciful man with a tender heart to all his relatives and Muslims, a rich, chaste man who gives in charity, and the people of Hell are five: the weak and the one who has no patience. To him, those who are among you as a follower, those who do not seek family or wealth, and a man who, in the morning, deceives you about your family and property, and a man who does not He has hidden greed, and if it strikes, it will take him away, and the immoral snort, and will remind him of miserliness and lying.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7757","7803 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Awf told us, he said: Hakim al-Athram told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, that Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir narrated to them, he said: Iyad bin Himar narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in a sermon He proposed to her: “Indeed, God has commanded me to teach you of what He has taught me this day. He said to me: Every property that I bestow upon My servants is lawful, and I have created My servants are all righteous, and indeed the devils came to them and caused them to turn away from their religion, and I prohibited for them what I had made lawful for them, and I commanded them That they associate with Me that for which I have not sent down authority, and I commanded them to change My character, and God looked at the people of the earth before He sent me. So he detested them, the Arabs and the non-Arabs, except for a remnant of the People of the Book. And God Almighty said: I have sent you only to test you and to test you. And I sent down to you a book that cannot be washed away by water, which you may read while asleep or awake, and God Almighty has revealed to me that I should burn the Quraysh. I said: When they gnaw at my head, they call it bread. Indeed, God says: Bring them out just as they have extracted you, and fight them, and we will fight you. And spend, I will spend. upon you, and send an army five times the size of it, and fight with those who obey you and those who disobey you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7758","7804 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom God has given wealth, and he spends it during the night and during the day, and a man to whom God has given the Qur’an, so he with it at times of the night and at times of the day.”"
"7759","7805 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom God has given the Qur’an, so he stands in prayer night and day, and a man to whom God has given wealth and destroy it in truth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7760","7806 Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, he said: Daoud bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, and Muhammad told us Bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, who said: I am Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Usama, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabbab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of Usayd bin Hudayr, “He was one of the best of people.” He recited a voice in the Qur’an. He said: I recited Surat Al-Baqarah, and a horse of mine was tied, and my son Yahya was lying near me, and he is a boy. So the horse moved around. around him, so I got up, having no concern for anyone but my son Yahya, and the mare was still, then I read, and the horse galloped, so I got up, having no concern for anyone but my son, then I read and the horse galloped, so I have nothing to worry about except my son. Then I read and the horse galloped, so I raised my head and saw something like the shape of a shadow. It was like a flash of light coming from the sky. He astonished me, so I remained silent. When I woke up, I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him. He said: “Read, O Abu Yahya,” and I said: “I have read,” and the horse galloped, so I stood up, worrying only about my son. He said: “Read, O Abu Hudair.” He said: “I have I read and raised my head, and behold, something like a canopy with lights in it. He said: Those angels approached your voice, and if you had read, the people would have come. They look at them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7761","7807 Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Ghazwan informed us, saying: Hafs bin Ghayath reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite Surat An-Nisa to me.” I said: Was it not revealed to you? He said: Yes, but I would like to That I could hear him from someone else, so I recited to him until I reached the message: How then when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as a witness against these, so he winked at me. Amer, so I raised my head, and his eyes were neglecting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7762","7808 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “He commanded me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited to him while he was on the pulpit, so I recited to him Surat An-Nisa, until when I reached the message: So how then? We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness against these. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, winked at me with his hand, and I looked at him, and his eyes \You're tearing up\"""""""
"7763","7809 Abdah bin Abdullah informed us, he said: Husayn informed us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Recite, then I opened Surat An-Nisa until I came to the words of God Almighty: So how if we come from all nation with a witness, and We have brought you as a witness over these. {41} On that day those who disbelieved and disobeyed the Messenger wish that the earth were leveled with them, and they would not conceal God. Recently {42}, he said: Then his eyes filled with tears, and he said: It is sufficient for us."
"7764","7810 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite to me.” I said: “I will recite and it was revealed to you.” He said: “I would love to hear it from someone else.” So I opened Surah An-Nisa, and when it was conveyed: So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as a witness against these people? He said: Then I saw his eyes. She was crying, so he said to me: “That’s enough for you.”"
"7765","7811 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah And some hadith, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite to me. I said: I recite to you and to you it was revealed. He said: I like to hear it from someone else, so I recited until I heard: How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as a witness against these people? He said: Hold on, and his eyes were streaming."
"7766","7812 Ali bin Khashram informed us, he said: Jesus informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Between us In the Levant, in Homs, and I was told: Read Surat Yusuf, so I read it, and a man said: This is not how it was revealed, so I said: By God, I have recited it to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: You have done well. While I was speaking to him, I smelled the scent of wine. I said: Do you deny the Book of God? And you drink wine, and by God, you will not leave until I flog you with punishment.”"
"7767","7813 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The example of a believer who reads the Qur’an is like a citrus fruit. Its taste and scent are good, and the example of a believer who does not He who recites the Qur’an is like a date, its taste is good but it has no smell, and the example of a hypocrite who recites the Qur’an is like basil, its smell is good but its taste is Bitter, and the likeness of the hypocrite who does not read the Qur’an is that of bitter melon, its taste and smell are vile. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7768","7814 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “The example of a believer who reads the Qur’an is that of a citrus tree, its scent is pleasant and its taste is pleasant, and the example of a believer who does not He who recites the Qur’an is like a date, which has no fragrance and its taste is sweet, and the example of a hypocrite who recites the Qur’an is like a basil, whose smell is pleasant. And its taste is bitter, and the likeness of the hypocrite who does not read the Qur’an is like the cocoa, it has no scent and its taste is bitter.”"
"7769","7815 Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: I am immortal, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Yusuf, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, he said: The people dispersed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and someone said to him: O Sheikh, tell us a hadith that you heard. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The first person to be judged is a man who was martyred. He was brought to him and his blessings were made known to him. He recognized them. He said: What did you do therein? He said: I fought.” In you until you were martyred. He said: You lied, but you fought so that it would be said: So-and-so is bold. It was said: Then he was ordered to be dragged and thrown into the Fire. And a man learned the Qur’an and taught it, and he recited the Qur’an, and it was brought to him, and he made known to him its blessings, and he recognized it. He said: What did you do in it? He said: I learned it in you And I taught him, and I recited the Qur’an to you. He said: You lied, but you learned so that it would be said: He is a scholar. It was said, and you read the Qur’an so that it would be said: He is a reader. It was said, then he commanded that he be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire, and a man whom God made abundantly abundantly, and gave him various kinds of wealth, So he was brought and he showed him his blessings, so he recognized them. He said: What did you do in it? He said: You did not leave any path in which you would like to be spent without spending in it. He said: You lied, but you did it so that it would be said: He is generous. It was said, then he was ordered to be dragged on his face until he was thrown into the Fire. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7770","7816 Abdul-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, And Muhammad bin Bishr said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Mukhlid said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever speaks about the Qur’an without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7771","7817 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever speaks about the Qur’an according to his opinion, or according to what he does not know, let him take his seat in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7772","7818 Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Ishaq Al-Hadrami, he said: Suhail bin Mihran Al-Quti told me, He said: Abu Imran Al-Juni narrated to us, on the authority of Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says in the Book of God according to his opinion and is correct.” \He made a mistake\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7773","7819 Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “A man came to the Messenger of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left Hunayn, and in Bilal’s garment was silver, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was holding And He gives to the people. He said: O Muhammad, be just. He said: Woe to you! Who will be just if I am not just? I have been disappointed and lost if I am not just. Omar said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, let me kill this hypocrite. He said: God forbid that people say that I kill “My companions, this man and his companions recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass from it as an arrow passes from the target.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7774","7820 Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us, as I read it while I was listening, on the authority of Yusuf bin Amr, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir say: “My eyes saw, and my ears heard, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. With a ji'ranah, and in Bilal's garment there was silver, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was taking it for the people and giving it to them. Then a man said: O Messenger of God. Be just. He said: Woe to you. Who will be just if I do not be just? I have failed and lost if I am not just. Omar said: Leave me, O Messenger of God. So I kill this hypocrite. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Lest people tell me that I am killing my companions. This man and his companions They recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats and throats. They walk away from religion as an arrow shoots away from its target.”"
"7775","7821 Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, and al-Harith ibn Miskin, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There will emerge a people who will despise your prayers along with their prayers. And your fasting is with their fasting, and your deeds are with their deeds. They recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass away from the debt as the arrow passes from the target. He looks at the blade and does not see anything, then he looks at the cup and does not see anything, then he looks at the feathers and does not see anything, and he wanders above.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7776","7822 Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yasir bin Amr, who said: I entered upon Sahl bin Hunaif, I said to him: Tell me what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Al-Hurriyah. He said: I will tell you what I heard from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I cannot say more, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he struck his hand toward the west, saying: From here will emerge a people who recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond their throats. They will leave the religion as an arrow leaves its target.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7777","7823 Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, saying: Ibn al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, saying: Yahya bin Sa’id and Al-Harith bin Miskin told me. Reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Hazim Al-Tammar, on the authority of Al-Bayadhi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the people while they were praying, and their voices rose as the recitation rose. He said: The one who prays speaks to his Lord, so let him see what he is speaking to Him with, and do not speak loudly to one another regarding the Qur’an. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7778","7824 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar informed us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, secluded himself in the mosque, and he heard them reciting aloud. While he was in a dome, he revealed the curtains and said: Indeed, each of you is in conversation with his Lord, so do not annoy one another, and do not exalt one another over others in Reciting, or he said: in prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7779","7825 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Anas bin Iyadh told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The Qur’an was revealed in seven letters, and hypocrisy in the Qur’an is blasphemy.”"
"7780","7826 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Maysara, he said: I heard the fight, He said: I heard Abdullah, he said: “I heard a man reciting a verse. I had heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting another verse, so I took With his hand, I brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his face changed and he said: Both of you are doers of good, do not disagree. therein, for those before you differed therein.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7781","7827 Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, he said: Dawud bin Muadh told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Jawni, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Rabah Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: “I migrated to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day, and he heard Two men were disagreeing about a verse from the Book of God. He came out with anger evident on his face and said: Those before you perished only because of their differences in \The Book\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7782","7828 Harun bin Zaid bin Yazid told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Farafafah, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy. On the authority of Jundub, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Unit upon the Qur’an whatever you agree upon, and if you disagree upon it, then stand up.” He told us about it another time, but he did not remove it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7783","7829 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Salam bin Abi Muti’ told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juni, on the authority of Jundub, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite the Qur’an whatever your hearts agree upon, and if you disagree upon it, then stand up.”"
"7784","7830 Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told me, he said: Muslim told us, he said: Harun bin Musa Al-Nahwi told us, he said: Abu Imran Al-Juni told us, on the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite the Qur’an whatever your hearts agree upon, then “If you differ concerning it, then depart from it.”"
"7785","7831 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Al-Azraq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aoun, on the authority of Abu Imran, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn al-Samit, he said: Omar said: “Recite the Qur’an what you have agreed upon, and if you disagree, then stand up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7786","Sulayman bin Ubayd Allah informed us, he said: Abu Amir told us, he said: Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali bin Hussein bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ahmad bin Al-Khalil told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Suleiman told me, he said: Amara bin Ghaziyah Al-Ansari told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Ali bin Hussein, speaking on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The miserly person is the one in whose presence I was mentioned, but he did not pray for me, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7787","7833 Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Salem, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Ali, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Abi Talib, that he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me these words in Al-Witr, he said: Say: O God, guide me among those whom You have guided, and bless for me what You have given, and take care of me among those whom You have taken charge of, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for You decree You will not be destroyed, and He will not humiliate those you are in charge of. You are blessed and exalted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7788","7834 Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: I am Wahb bin Jarir, he said: I am my father, on the authority of Ya’la bin Hakim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out during his illness in which he died, tying his head with a rag, and he sat on the pulpit, then praised.” God Almighty, the Almighty, praised him, then said: He is not one of the people who trusted me with his life and his wealth more than Abu Bakr bin Abi Quhafa, even if I were “Taking a friend. I would not have taken Abu Bakr as a friend, but the friend of Islam is better. Block for me every window in the mosque other than the door of Abu Bakr.”"
"7789","7835 Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, saying: I am al-Qanabi, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Hunayn, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people trusted me with regard to his company and wealth, Abu Bakr, even if I were “Taking a friend. I did not take Abu Bakr as a friend, but they are brothers in Islam. Not a single person will remain in the mosque except the friend of Abu Bakr.”"
"7790","7836 Azhar bin Jamil informed us, he said: I am Khaled bin Al-Harith, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abu Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If I had taken a friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr is a friend, but he is my brother and friend, and God has taken your friend as a friend.”"
"7791","7837 Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas. On the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, I disavow the fault of every friend of his, even if I were taking a friend. “I have not taken Ibn Abi Quhafa as a friend, but your companion is the friend of God.”"
"7792","Muhammad ibn Issa informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Aas, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, Which people are most beloved to you? He said: Aisha. I said: Not one of the women. He said: Her father. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7793","Abdul Rahman bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, he said: Yazid told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Who among you has woken up fasting today? Abu Bakr said: I have. He said: Who has fed a poor person today? He said: Abu Bakr: I. He said: Who among you attended a funeral today? Abu Bakr said: I. He said: Who among you visited a sick person today? Bakr: “I”"
"7794","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told me, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever spends two pairs of things in the way of God, he will be called From the gates of Paradise: This is better, and Paradise has gates, so whoever is among the people of prayer will be called from the gate of prayer, and whoever is among the people of jihad Abu Bakr: Is there any necessity for the one who is called from those gates? Should he be called from one of them, O Messenger of God? He said: “Yes, and I hope it is?” \from them\"""""""
"7795","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Salama bin Nabit, on the authority of Nu’aym, on the authority of Nabit, on the authority of Salim bin Ubaid, he said: “And he was one of the people of the Suffah. He said: The Ansar said: Among us is a leader, and among you is a leader. Umar said: Two swords in one sheath, so no They reconciled, then he took Abu Bakr’s hand and said: Who has these three? When he said to his friend, “Who is his friend?” when they were in the cave Who are they? Indeed, God is with us. With whom? Then he pledged allegiance to him, then he said: “Pledge allegiance,” so the people gave the best and most beautiful pledge of allegiance."
"7796","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Ghazwan told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We are not benefited by wealth, Abu Bakr’s wealth is of no benefit to us.” He said: Then Abu Bakr cried and said: Did I and my property are yours only.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7797","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abu Dawud al-Hafari Omar bin Saad, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “While a man was driving a cow, he wanted to He would ride it, and she said: We were not created for this, but rather we were created to be plowed over by us. So those around him said: Glory be to God, Glory be to God, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I, Abu Bakr, and Omar believed in him, and what were they? Then he said: While a man was among his sheep, he came The wolf took a sheep from her, and the shepherd followed it to take it. The wolf said: How will she do on the day of the wild beast, the day when she has no shepherd but me? Those around him said: Glory be to God, Glory be to God, and he said: I believed in him, and Abu Bakr, and Omar, and what they were.” Then"
"7798","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Issa, who is the son of Al-Qasim bin Sami’, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Omar told us, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached the people and said: While a man was driving a cow He wanted to ride it, so she approached him and said: We were not created for this, we were created for ploughing. So those around him said: Glory be to Him. By God, a cow spoke, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I believed in him, and Abu Bakr and Omar, but not them, then he said: He said A man: While I was among the sheep, a wolf came and took a sheep. I asked for it and took it from him, and he said to me: How can it be on the seventh day, when there is no It will have a shepherd other than me. They said: Glory be to God. A wolf spoke, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I believed in him, and so did Abu Bakr. And Omar, not then (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7799","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left the prayer and went to his companions and said: While a man was driving a cow, So he began to ride it, so she approached him and said: We were not created for this, we were created for plowing. So those around him said: Glory be to God, Glory be to God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I believed in him, I, Abu Bakr, and Omar, and while a man was in His sheep, when the wolf came and took a sheep from his sheep, and asked for its shepherd. When he caught up with him, he pronounced it, and approached him, and said: Who has it? On the seventh day, it will not have a shepherd other than me. Then those around him said: Glory be to God, Glory be to God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So I am. I, Abu Bakr, and Omar believed in him.”"
"7800","Suleiman bin Dawud Al-Mahri told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa’id bin told me Al-Musayyab and Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman, that they heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “While a man He was driving a cow on which he had loaded. The cow turned to him and said: I was not created for this, but we were created for plowing. So the people said: Glory be to Him. God marveled at a speaking cow. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I believe in him, as do Abu Bakr and Omar.” Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We saw a shepherd among his sheep, except for a wolf, which took a sheep. The shepherd asked him to rescue it from him, so he turned around. The wolf came to him, and he said: Who has hers on the seventh day when she has no shepherd other than me? The people said: Glory be to God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I, Abu Bakr, and Omar believe in that.”"
"7801","7847 Muhammad bin Adam told me, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, He says: “Umar was placed on his bed, people surrounded him, praying over him and making supplications before he was taken up, and I was among them, and only a man took care of me. My shoulders were behind me, so I turned to Ali, praying for mercy for Omar, then he said: I have not left behind anyone more beloved to me than to do something like his to God than you. By God, I wish that God would place you with your two companions, and that is because I used to hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I, Abu Bakr, and Omar went, and I, Abu Bakr, and Omar entered, and I, Abu Bakr, and Omar went out, even if I “I think that God will place you with them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7802","7848 Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “While I was sleeping, you saw me on a grave with a bucket on top of it, so I removed from it what God wished, then Ibn Abi Quhafa took it, and he removed one or two sins, and there was weakness in his removal, and may God forgive him, then the bucket moved west. Then Omar Ibn Al-Khattab took it, and I have never seen a genius among the people be as capable as Ibn Al-Khattab, to the point that he hit the people with a curse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7803","7849 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: I am Abdul Aziz bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Othman, he said: Amr bin Al-Aas told me, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed me to command the army of Dhat al-Salasil, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of God, which of the people is most beloved to you? He said: Aisha. I said: Who are the men? He said: Her father. I said: Then who? He said: Then Omar. He counted some men. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Some of Abu Uthman’s letters were not correct."
"7804","7850 Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: I am Waki’, he said: Abu Al-Umays told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested and did not appoint a successor.” She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If “If I had appointed anyone as successor, I would have appointed Abu Bakr and Omar as successors.”"
"7805","7851 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: I am Al-Layth bin Sa’d, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There were scholars of hadith scholars among my nation, but if there is anyone among my nation, then Umar ibn Al-Khattab"
"7806","7852 Muhammad ibn Rafi’ and Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad informed us, saying: Suleiman ibn Dawud told us, he said: I am Ibrahim, he is the son of Sa’d, on the authority of his father. On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There were among the nations before you people who spoke of hadith, If there is one of them in my nation, it is Omar bin Al-Khattab.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7807","7853 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am my father, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, He said: Abu Umamah bin Sahl told me that he heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “While I While I was asleep, I saw people being shown to me wearing shirts, some that reached the size of the breast, and some that reached less than that, and Omar ibn Al-Khattab was wearing a shirt dragging him. They said: What did you explain that, O Messenger of God? He said: Religion? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7808","7854 Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “While I was sleeping, I saw that I had been brought a cup, so I drank from it until I saw the irrigation coming out, then I gave my bounty Omar. They said: What did you explain, O Messenger of God? He said: Knowledge? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7809","7855 Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah Ibn Omar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “While I was sleeping, a cup of milk was brought to me and I drank from it.” I even saw watering running through my nails. Then I was given Umar’s bounty. They said: What did you explain that? He said: Knowledge."
"7810","7856 Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Shuaib bin Harb told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was shown that I had entered Paradise, and when I shortened In its courtyard there was a female slave, so I said: Who is this for, O Gabriel? He said: This is for Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, so I wanted to enter it and look. To him, I mentioned your jealousy, and he said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God, or should I be jealous of you? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7811","7857 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, and Ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “I entered Paradise, and I saw therein a palace or a house, so I said: Who is this for? They said: To Omar bin Al-Khattab, so I wanted to enter it.” Then I mentioned your jealousy, O Abu Hafs, but I did not enter it. Then Omar cried and said: Am I jealous of you, O Messenger of God? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7812","7858 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I entered Paradise, and behold, I saw a palace of gold. I said: Who is this for? They said: For a man from the Quraysh, so what? It prevents me from entering it, O Ibn Al-Khattab, except for what I know of your jealousy. He said: And should I be jealous of you, O Messenger of God? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7813","7859 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: I am Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I entered Paradise, then I saw a palace of gold. I said: Whose palace is this? They said: It belongs to a young man from Quraysh, so I thought that I was him, so I said: Who is he? They said: Omar bin Al-Khattab. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7814","7860 Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told me, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Amr bin Uthman told me, he said Baqiyya narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, he said: Al-Zuhri informed me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “While we were sitting at The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: While I was sleeping, I saw in Paradise a woman performing ablution next to a palace, so I said: Whose palace is this? They said: For Omar, so I mentioned his jealousy, so I turned away, and Omar cried while he was in the assembly, and said: May Abu Aghar be upon you. Messenger of God\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7815","7861 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Had, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman bin Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, said: “Umar ibn al-Khattab asked permission to go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there were some Ansar women with him who were talking to him. They used to do it a lot, raising their voices. When Omar asked for permission, they quickly took off the veil. Omar entered and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was laughing. He said: May God make your years laugh, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was astonished by these women who were with me. When they heard With your voice, they rushed to wear the veil, and Omar said: And you have more right that they should fear, then Omar said: That is, the enemies of themselves, did you fear me and you did not fear? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: Yes, you are harsher and harsher than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, Satan never met you on a path other than your path.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7816","7862 Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my uncle told us, he said: I am my father, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, that Abu Salamah Ibn Abdul-Rahman Ibn Awf told him that Abd al-Rahman Ibn Nafi’ Ibn Abd al-Harith al-Khuza’i informed him that Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was in a wall in Medina, at the end of a well, with his feet dangling, so he knocked on the door.” Abu Bakr, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Give him permission and give him good tidings of Paradise, so he did so, so Abu Bakr entered and let him spread his legs. Then Omar knocked on the door, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Give him permission and give him good news of Paradise, so he did, then Othman knocked on the door. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Give him permission, and give him good tidings of Paradise, and he will face calamity."
"7817","7863 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Ismail, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Abdul Harith Al-Khuza’i said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered one of the walls of the city and said to Bilal: Hold the door. Then Abu Bakr, so he asked for permission while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting on the stand with his legs extended. Then Bilal came and said: This is Abu Bakr. He asked for permission, and he said: Give him permission, and give him good news of Paradise, so he came and sat down, and dangled his legs on the stand with him, then he knocked on the door, and he came Bilal, and he said: This is Omar asking for permission. He said: Give him permission, and give him good tidings of Paradise. He said: Then he came and sat with him on the stand, and dangled his legs. Then he knocked on the door, and Bilal came and said: This is Uthman seeking permission. He said: Give him permission, and give him good tidings of Paradise, and with it a calamity. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7818","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Uthman ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in a wall, and a man opened the door, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Open.” for him, and give him good tidings of Paradise, so I opened for him and gave him good tidings of Paradise, and behold, Abu Bakr. Then another one opened, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Open for him, and give him good tidings of Paradise, and behold, Omar. Then another one opened for him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Open for him. And he gave him good tidings of Paradise for his calamity, so I opened and gave him good tidings of Paradise, and I told him what he said. He said: God is the one who seeks help. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7819","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Yahya, he said: Ibn Abi Orouba told us, and Amr bin Ali told us, he said: I am Yazid, and he is the son of Zurai’ and Yahya said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went up to Uhud, and Abu Bakr was with him. And Omar and Othman, so he shook at them and hit him with his foot, and said: Stand firm, for over you is only a prophet, a truthful, and two witnesses.” The wording is by Amr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7820","7866 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. One day, he said: “Who among you has seen a vision?” Then a man said: “I saw a balance come down from the sky, and you were weighed.” And Abu Bakr, so you preferred Abu Bakr, then Omar was weighed, and Abu Bakr, so Abu Bakr preferred, then Omar and Uthman were weighed, Omar decided, then the scales were lifted, and I saw hatred on the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7821","7867 Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, a servant Al-Ansar, he said: I heard Zayd bin Arqam saying: “The first to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” and he said: In another place: the first “Whoever submits to Islam, Ali.”"
"7822","7868 Bishr bin Hilal informed us, he said: I am Ja’far, on the authority of Ibn Sulaiman, he said: I am Harb bin Shaddad, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, launched the Battle of Tabuk, he left Ali in Medina, and they said about him: He bored him. He hated his company, so Ali followed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he caught up with him on the road. He said: “O Messenger of God, you left me behind in Medina with Offspring and women until they said: He bored him and hated his company. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: O Ali: I have only left you in charge of my family. You are pleased to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7823","7869 Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyib, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: You are to me as Aaron was to Moses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7824","7870 Ali bin Muslim told us, he said: Yusuf bin Yaqoub Al-Majishun Abu Salamah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir informed me, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab said: I asked Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas: “Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to Ali: You are in the same position as me.” Aaron is from Moses, except that he is not with me, or is there a prophet after me? He said: Yes, I heard him. I said: Did you hear him? So he put his two fingers into his ears. He said: Yes, otherwise they will remain silent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7825","7871 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: I am Muhammad. He said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, succeeded Ali bin Abi Talib in the Battle of Tabuk, and he said: O Messenger of God, will you leave me in charge of women?” And the boys. He said: Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7826","7872 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: I am Muhammad, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ibrahim bin Saad narrating On the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said to Ali: “Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7827","7873 Amr bin Ali informed us. He said: I am Yahya bin Saeed. He said: I am Musa al-Juhani. He said: I entered upon Fatima bint Ali. He said to her: Rafiqi: Do you have anything confirmed about your father? She said: Asma bint Umays told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ali: “You are to me what Aaron was to Moses, except “There will be no prophet after me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7828","7874 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: I am Abu Muawiyah, he said: I am Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever I am his guardian, then Ali is his guardian.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7829","7875 Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: I am Abd al-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyeh, he said: Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Buraidah, said: “I went out with Ali to Yemen, and I saw a faintness from him, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So I mentioned Ali, so I looked at him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made his face change. He said: O Buraida, aren’t you Who has more right to the believers than they themselves? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7830","7876 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: I am Ja’far, and he is Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Yazid Al-Rashk, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of Imran Ibn Husayn said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ali is from me, and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me.”"
"7831","7877 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Adam, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Habashi bin Junada told me Al-Saluli, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ali is from me, and I am from him, and no one can perform on my behalf except me or Ali.”"
"7832","7878 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: Habib bin Abi told us. Thabit, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage and descended on Ghadir Khumm He ordered a group of people to stand up, then he said: It is as if I had been called and I responded. Indeed, I have left among you two weighty matters, one of which is greater than the other: the Book of God. And my family, my family, so see how you will leave me behind them, for they will not separate until they return to the basin. Then he said: Indeed, God is my master. And I am the guardian of every believer. Then he took Ali’s hand and said: Whoever I was the guardian of, this is his guardian. Oh God, befriend whoever befriends him, and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him. So I said to Zaid: I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: There was not a man in the plagues but saw it with his own eyes and heard it with his ears. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7833","7879 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, he said: I am Ya’qub, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: Sahl bin Sa’id informed us, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said on the Day of Khaybar: “I will give this banner tomorrow to a man at whose hands God will grant victory, who loves God and His Messenger, and God loves him.” And His Messenger. When the morning came, the people went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, all of them hoping to be given it. He said: Where is Ali bin Abi Talib? They said: He, O Messenger of God, suffers from his eyes. He said: So they sent for him, and he was brought. He spit in his eyes and prayed for him, and he was healed until It was as if he had no ailment, so he gave him the standard, and Ali said: O Messenger of God, I will fight them until they are like us. He said: Follow your messengers. Until you go down to their square, then invite them to Islam. By God, for God to guide a man through you is better for you than to have red camels.”"
"7834","7880 Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Omar bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, he said: I am Mu’tamar bin Sulayman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger Or he said: God and His Messenger love him, so he called Ali, and he was gray-haired, so God opened his hands to me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7835","7881 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Yazid bin Kaysan told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will hand the flag today to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him.” The people, and he said: Where is Ali? They said: He complained about his eyes, so he called for him, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spit on his palms, then wiped my eyes with them. Ali, and the banner was handed over to him, and God granted him victory on that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7836","7882 I read about Muhammad bin Sulayman, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, and he did not mention it once, on the authority of his father, he said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and some people were sitting with him. So Ali entered, and when he entered, they left, and when they came out, they blamed each other, and they said: By God, he did not take us out and let him in. So they returned and entered, and he said: By God, he did not take him out. I brought it in and brought you out. The Prophet of God brought it in and brought you out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7837","7883 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Ali, he said: “By the One who split the grain and created the breath, it is the covenant of the unlettered Prophet with me that no one will love me except a believer, and no one will hate me except a hypocrite.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7838","7884 And while Ahmad bin Mani’ read to us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, he said: I heard Abu Dharr swore an oath, “This verse was revealed about those who dueled on the day of Badr: Hamza, Ali, and Ubaidah bin Al-Harith. Utbah, Shaybah ibn Rabi’ah, and Al-Walid ibn Utbah.”"
"7839","7885 Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: I am Yazid, he said: I am the Awwam, he said: Saeed bin Jumhan told me, on the authority of the ship of the servant of the Messenger of Allah God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The caliphate in my nation is thirty years, then kingship after that,” he said: So we succumbed, and we found Abu Bakr, Omar, Uthman, and Ali.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7840","7886 Abdah bin Abdullah and Al-Qasim bin Zakaria informed us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Sayyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Akhnas, on the authority of Sa`id bin Zayd, who said: “Hira’ was shaken, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Stand firm, Hira, for there is no one against you except a prophet, or a truthful, or a martyr, and upon him are the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, and Omar. And Uthman, and Ali, and Talha, and Al-Zubayr, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas, and me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7841","7887 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: I am Abdul Wahhab, he said: I am Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “He did not follow Shoes, nor riding on football, nor riding on mounts, nor stepping on the dirt after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is better than Ja’far bin Abi Talib.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7842","7888 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I am Yazid bin Harun, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Amir, he said: Ibn Umar said, “When he greeted Ali Abdullah bin Jaafar said: Peace be upon you, O son of the two-winged one."
"7843","7889 Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Ali informed me, saying: My father informed us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Aswad. Ibn Shayban, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Samir, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ascended The pulpit, so he ordered the caller to call out: Prayer is unified, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The news is confirmed, the news is confirmed, the news is confirmed, isn’t it? Shall I tell you about this invading army of yours? They set off until they met the enemy, but Zaid was wounded and martyred, so they asked forgiveness for him, then he was taken away. Major General Jaafar attacked the people and was killed as a martyr. I bear witness to his martyrdom, so ask forgiveness for him. Then Major General Abdullah bin Rawaha, so he remained firm on his feet until he was injured and became a martyr, so they asked forgiveness for him. Then they took General Khalid bin Al-Walid, who was not one of the princes, so he raised The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, touched his fingers and said: Oh God, this is one of your swords, so be victorious with it. On that day, Khalid was called the sword of God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7844","7890 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: I am Wahb bin Jarir, he said: I am my father, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub, speaking on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Saad, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Ja’far, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave three people to the Ja’far family to come to them, then he came to them and said: No.” You will cry, my brother, after today. Then he said: Bring me my brother’s sons. We were brought as if we were chicks, so he ordered our heads to be shaved. Then he said: As for Muhammad, He resembled our uncle Abu Talib, and as for Abdullah, he resembled me in character and character. Then he took me by the hand and said: Oh God, succeed Ja’far in His family, and bless Abdullah in the pledge of his oath, O God, succeed Jafar in his family, and bless Abdullah in the pledge of his oath, O God, appoint Ja’far as successor to his family, and bless Abdullah in the pledge of his oath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7845","7891 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, saying: I am Abu Dawud, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith, who said: “I was with Abu Bakr when he passed by Al-Hasan, and he placed him on his neck, then said: By Abu Bakr, he is like the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. There was no resemblance to Ali, and Ali was with him, so he started laughing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7846","7892 Amr bin Ali informed us. He said: I am Yahya. He said: I am Ismail. He said: I am Abu Juhayfah. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said hello, and Al-Hasan bin Ali looked like him.”"
"7847","7893 Ali bin Al-Hussein informed us, he said: I am Umayyah bin Khalid, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Al-Hassan on his shoulders, and he was saying: Oh God, I love this, so love him.”"
"7848","7894 Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Al-Hasan: “Oh God, I love him, so love him, and love whoever loves him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7849","7895 Ismail bin Masoud informed us, saying: I am Khalid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, meaning Anas. He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivering a sermon with Al-Hasan on his thigh, and he spoke as he pleased, then He approaches him, and he kisses him, and says: Oh God, I love him, so I love him, and he says: I hope that there will be reconciliation through him between two groups of my nation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7850","7696 Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id informed us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace while he was embracing Al-Hassan, and he said: This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God will bring about reconciliation through his hands between two groups of Muslims.”"
"7851","7897 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Khaled, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: meaning Anas bin Malik. He said: “I entered, or perhaps I entered, upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein were turning around.” On his stomach, he said: And he says: Rayhantai is from this nation. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7852","7898 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahhaf, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me. Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein.”"
"7853","7899 Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Marwan, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who is the son of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the lords of the youth of the people of Paradise, except for the two sons of my cousin Jesus.” The son of Maryam, and Yahya bin Zakaria.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7854","7900 Al-Hasan bin Ishaq told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: I am Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, and when he prostrated, Al-Hasan jumped up, and Al-Hussein was on his back, and when he wanted them to be prevented, he signaled So they called them, and when he prayed, he placed them in his lap, then said: Whoever loves me, let him love these two. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7855","7901 Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id informed us, saying: I am Yahya, on the authority of Al-Taymi, and Al-Hasan ibn Qazah informed us, on the authority of Sufyan ibn Habib, He said: I am Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to take me and Al-Hasan bin Ali. He says: Oh God, love them, for I love them."
"7856","7902 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Worship, he said: I heard Abu Dharr swear: “This verse was revealed: These are two adversaries who disputed about their Lord, about Ali and Hamza. Ubaid bin Al-Harith, Shaybah bin Rabi’ah, Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and Al-Walid bin Utba disputed on the day of Badr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7857","7903 Ahmad bin Sulayman informed us, saying: I am Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, that he heard Saeed bin Jubayr, saying: Ibn Abbas told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Al-Abbas is from me, and I am from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7858","7904 أَخْبَرَنَا حُمَيْدُ بْنُ مَخْلَدٍ ، قَالَ : أنا عَلِيُّ بْنُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ، قَالَ : ثنا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ طَلْحَةَ التَّيْمِيُّ ، قَالَ : ثنا نَافِعٌ أَبُو سُهَيْلٍ ، On the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sa`d bin Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib: This is Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, the best-handed and most generous of the Quraysh.”"
"7859","7905 Zakaria ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hayyan al-Taymi Yahya ibn Sa`id ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan said: Husayn bin Samurah bin Umar bin Muslim and I went to Zayd bin Arqam, and we sat with him, and Husayn said: O Zaid, tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and what you witnessed with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose with water. He is called Kham, so he thanked God, praised Him, exhorted, and mentioned, then he said: Now, O people, I am only a human being about to come to me. Messenger of my Lord, so I will answer him, and I am leaving among you the two burdens: the first of which is the Book of God, in which is guidance and light, and whoever adheres to it and embraces it will be upon guidance, and whoever makes a mistake and abandons it has gone astray. And my family. I remind you of God regarding my family three times. Husayn said: So who The members of his household, O Zaid? Aren’t his wives among his household? He said: Yes, his wives are among his household, but his household are those for whom charity is forbidden. He said: Who are they? He said: The family of Ali, the family of Aqeel, the family of Jafar, and the family of Abbas."
"7860","7906 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: I am Abu Awanah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: Al-Muttalib bin Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib told me that Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib “entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He greeted me angrily, while I was with him. He said: What made you angry? He said: O Messenger of God, what do we have to do with the Quraysh? If they meet, they meet each other. With happy faces, and when they met us, they met us with anything other than that. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry until his face turned red, then he said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, faith will not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for the sake of God and for His Messenger. Then he said: O people, whoever harmed my uncle, He has harmed me, but a man’s uncle is like his father.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7861","7907 Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Nadr told us, he said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim told us, he said: I am Warqa bin Omar al-Yashkari, he said: I heard Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the toilet, so I put water for him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came. He greeted him and said: Who made this? I said: Ibn Abbas. He said: Oh God, grant him success. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7862","7908 Muhammad bin Hatim informed us, he said: I am Al-Qasim bin Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He prayed for me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him to give me wisdom twice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7863","7909 Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: I am Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger swore to me He, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to his chest and said: O God, teach him wisdom."
"7864","7910 Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Hassan told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “When Zainab's period of waiting had ended. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Zaid, there is no one more trustworthy in me and more secure in my eyes than you, so remember her. Ali, so I went, and behold, she was baking her dough, and when I saw her, my heart became so great that I could not look at her when I learned that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned her, so I turned my back to her and said: O Zainab, give me good news. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me. He reminds you, so she said: I will not do anything unless I command my Lord. So she got up to her mosque, and the Qur’an was revealed and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. peace be upon him, then he entered upon her without permission.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7865","7911 Ali bin Hajar informed us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He sent a delegation, and Usama bin Zaid was appointed over them, and some people challenged his command, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you challenge His authority, for you were disputing his father’s authority before, and I swear by God, if he is worthy of the authority, and if he is one of the most beloved people to me And this is for the most beloved of people to me after him.”"
"7866","7912 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Ubaid, he said: I am Wael bin Dawud, he said: I heard Al-Bahi narrating that Aisha, She used to say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never sent Zaid bin Haritha to an army without giving him command over them, even if he remained after him. To appoint him as his successor.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Al-Bahi’s name is Abdullah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7867","7913 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: I am Ibn Abi Adiy, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, he said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, takes my hand and the hand of Al-Hasan and says: Oh God, I love them, so I love them.”"
"7868","7914 Siwar bin Abdullah bin Siwar told us, he said: I am Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Abu Tamimah speaking, on the authority of my father Othman, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to take me and make me sit on his thigh, and Al-Hasan bin Ali on his other thigh, then he placed us down, then he said: Oh God, love them, for I love them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7869","7915 Harun bin Musa told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Falih, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem bin Abdullah said: Abdullah said: “The people challenged the leadership of Ibn Zayd, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and said: If you challenge the leadership of Ibn Zayd, You were challenging the emirate of his father before him, and I swear to God, if he is worthy of the emirate, and if it belongs to the one whom all people love to me, “This is the most beloved of people to me after him, so treat him well, for he is among your best.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7870","7916 Amr ibn Yahya ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: I am Al-Mu’affa, he said: I am Zuhayr, he said: I am Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Salim ibn Abd God, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded Osama, and he heard that people were disgracing Osama and slandering him.” In his emirate, he said: You are disgracing Osama, and you are challenging his emirate, and you did that to his father before, even if he was of good character. For the emirate, even if he is the most beloved of all people to me, and this son of his after him is the most beloved of people to me, so treat him well, for he is one of Your choice.” Salem said: I never heard Abdullah bin Omar narrate this hadith except that he said: God forbid, Fatima."
"7871","7917 Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told us, he said: This is Abu Usama, he said: I am Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asma The daughter of Abu Bakr, she said: I saw Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl, with his back resting on the Kaaba, and he was saying: “What of you today?” Someone follows the religion of Abraham other than me, and he used to say: My God is the God of Abraham, and my religion is the religion of Abraham. He said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned it. He said: On the Day of Resurrection, a nation will be raised alone between me and Jesus. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7872","Musa ibn Hizam narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Harithah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah"
"7873","7919 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I am Affan, he said: I am Wahib, he said: Musa bin Uqba told me, he said: I am safe, that he heard Abdullah bin Omar, narrating on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He met Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl at the foot of Baldah before he The revelation came down to him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, presented to him a plate containing meat, but he refused to eat from it, then he said: I do not I eat of what you sacrifice to your idols, and I do not eat except that on which the name of God is mentioned.” This was narrated by Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him"
"7874","7920 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zalim, he said: I entered upon Saeed. Ibn Zayd, so I said: “Aren’t you amazed at this oppressor, who set up preachers to insult Ali?” So he said: Or did they do it? I bear witness to the nine that they In Paradise, and if I had testified about the tenth, I would have told the truth. We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on Hira’, and he moved, and said: Hira’a stand still. No one is responsible for you except a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr. I said: And who was in Hira? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr. And Omar, and Uthman, and Ali, and Talha, and Al-Zubayr, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and Saad. We said: Who is the tenth? He said: “I am.” He told us Ishaq bin Ibrahim said: I am Ibn Idris. He said: I heard Husayn narrating a similar chain of transmission with this chain of transmission. Hilal bin Yasaf did not hear it. From Abdullah bin Zalim, Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Ubaid bin Saeed, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zalim, on the authority of Saeed bin Zayd, who said: Hira moved, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said hello, and he mentioned something like it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7875","7921 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: I am Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I am Sadaqah bin Al-Muthanna, he said: My grandfather Riyah bin Al-Harith told me that Saeed bin Zaid said: “I bear witness against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to what my ears heard and my heart understood, and that I would not narrate to him He lied and asked me about him when I met him, that he said: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Omar is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, and Othman is in Paradise. Talhah will be in Paradise, Al-Zubayr will be in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman bin Awf will be in Paradise, Saad bin Malik will be in Paradise, and the ninth of the believers. If I wanted to name him, I would have named him. Then the people of the mosque started calling for him, O companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Who is the ninth? He said: You called upon me by God Almighty, for I am the ninth of the believers, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the tenth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7876","7922 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: I am Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Humaid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Awf said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Omar is in Paradise, and Othman is in Paradise. And Ali is in Paradise, and he said again: Ali is in Paradise, Othman is in Paradise, Talha is in Paradise, Al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Abd Al-Rahman bin Awf will be in Paradise, Saad bin Abi Waqqas will be in Paradise, and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah will be in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7877","7923 Muhammad bin Aban informed us, saying: I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Fudaik, on the authority of Musa bin Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Wahb bin Zam’a, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid, on the authority of his father, that Saeed bin Zaid told him in a group that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ten will be in Paradise: Abu Bakr, Omar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, and Abdul-Rahman.” And Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah, and Saad bin Abi Waqqas, so he counted these nine, then he remained silent about the tenth, so the people said: We seek you. By God, O Abu Al-A'war, you are the tenth. He said: When you called upon me by God, Abu Al-A'war will be in Paradise. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7878","7924 Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: I am Qasim, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud said: “And the two companions of Najran came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they wanted to curse him, and one of them said: No.” You curse him, for by God, if he were a prophet, perhaps we would not succeed, nor would our successors after us. They said to him: We will give you what you ask for, so send an honest man with us. Truly, Amen. So the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked to her and said: Get up, O Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah. When he stood up, he said: This “Amin of this nation” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7879","7925 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abu Dawud al-Hafari, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silah, on the authority of Hudhayfah He said: “Al-Aqib and Al-Sayyid, who were companions of Najran, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Send with us a truly trustworthy and trustworthy man. The people knelt down, and he said: Get up, Abu Ubaidah."
"7880","7926 Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr and Ismail bin Masoud told us on the authority of Khalid, who said: Shu’bah told us that Abu Ishaq He told them, saying: I heard Silah bin Zufar saying: I heard Hudhayfah mentioning that the people of Najran came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: Send over us a trustworthy man. He said: I will certainly send over you a truly trustworthy and trustworthy man. So the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked forward to her. He said hello, so he sent Abu Ubaidah.” Humayd ibn Masada told us, in his hadith on the authority of Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: I am Khalid."
"7881","7927 And Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Ibn Abi Adiy, on the authority of Khalid, Abu Qalaba said, Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Every nation has a trustworthy person, and our trustworthy one, O nation, is Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.”"
"7882","7928 Imran bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abdul-Warith, he said: I am Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aisha, I said: “Which of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was he most beloved to? She said: Abu Bakr, then Omar, then Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah. I said: Then who remained silent?"
"7883","7929 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim and Musa bin Abdul Rahman informed us, and the pronunciation is his, he said: I am Ja’far bin Aoun, on the authority of my father Umays, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, said: I heard Aisha, “I was asked who the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was as successor, if He succeeded? She said: Abu Bakr. Then she was asked: Who is after Abu Bakr? She said: Omar. Then she was asked: Who is after Omar? Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, then she concluded with this. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7884","7930 Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majlaz, on the authority of Qays ibn `Ubad, he said: I heard Abu Dharr swear an oath, “This verse was revealed: These are two adversaries who disputed about their Lord, about Ali. And Hamza, Ubaidah bin Al-Harith, Shaybah bin Rabi’ah, and Utbah bin Rabi’ah disputed on the day of Badr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7885","7931 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Abdul-Wahid, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: Al-Hurr bin Sayyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Al-Akhnas said: Saeed bin Zaid stood up and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Abu Bakr is in Paradise. Omar is in Paradise, Othman is in Paradise, Talha is in Paradise, Al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Saad is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf is in Paradise. Paradise, and if I wanted to name the ninth, I would have named it, so we thought it meant the same.”"
"7886","7932 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf. On the authority of Abdullah bin Zalim, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah proposed a speech and insulted Ali, so Sa’id bin Zayd said: “I bear witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, I heard him say: Stand firm, Hira, for there is no one upon you except a prophet, or a truthful, or a martyr, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is upon him. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, Abu Bakr, Omar, Othman, Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, Sa’d, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Sa’id ibn \Zaid\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7887","7933 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told me, he said: Qasim Al-Jarmi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, On the authority of So-and-so bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zalim, he said: I received Saeed bin Zaid, and he said: “Our princes order us to curse our brothers.” And we do not curse them, but we say: May God forgive them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: After me there will be tribulations in which there will be and there will be. Then a man said: If we reach it, we will surely perish. He said: Killing is sufficient for you. He said: Then a man came and said: I loved Ali but I did not love him. He never said anything, he said: I loved a man from the people of Paradise, then he started speaking, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, And Omar, and Uthman, and Ali, and Talha, and Al-Zubayr, and Abdul-Rahman, and Saad, and if you wish, you can be counted as the tenth, meaning himself, so the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Hold Hira, for there is no one against you except a prophet, or a truthful, or a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7888","7934 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, was in Hira’, he and Abu Bakr, Omar, Othman, Ali, Talha, and Al-Zubayr, and the rock moved, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Guide him, for there is no one upon you except a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7889","7935 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: I am Ibn Dris, he said: I am Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zalim, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zalim, and Sufyan mentioned a man between him and Abdullah bin Zalim, He said: I heard Saeed bin Zaid, he said: “When Muawiyah came to Kufa, Mughirah bin Shu’bah appointed preachers to address Ali, so he took my hand. Saeed bin Zaid, and he said: Don’t you see this oppressor who orders the cursing of a man from the people of Paradise, so I bear witness against the nine that they are in Paradise? And if I had witnessed the tenth, I would have said: Who are the nine? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: While he was in Hira’, prove that there is nothing wrong with you. A prophet, a truthful person, or a martyr. He said: Who are the nine? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman. And Ali, Talha, Al-Zubayr, Saad, and Abdul-Rahman. I said: From the tenth. He said: I. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7890","7936 Muawiyah bin Salih informed us, he said: I am Zakaria bin Adiy, he said: I am Ali bin Mushar, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Marwan, he said: No, I think he is being blamed against us. He said: Uthman was struck by the shudders of the Sunnah of slander, so he was told: He became a successor, and he said: So they said: Al-Zubayr. He said: By God, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if it was for the last of them and the most beloved of them to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"7891","7937 Hajib bin Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hurr bin Sayyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Akhnas, who said: I witnessed Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl with Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah. He mentioned something from Ali, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Ten of the Quraysh will be in Paradise: Abu Bakr will be in Paradise, Omar will be in Paradise, Ali will be in Paradise, and Othman will be in Paradise.” Talhah will be in Paradise, Al-Zubayr will be in Paradise, Abdul Rahman will be in Paradise, Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas will be in Paradise, and Sa’id bin Zaid bin Amr"
"7892","7938 Al-Qasim bin Zakaria informed us, saying: I am Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, and Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who will bring us the news of the people?” Al-Zubayr said: I, so the Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “For every prophet there is a disciple, and my disciple is Al-Zubair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7893","7939 Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Zubayr is my cousin, and my disciple from my nation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7894","7940 Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym informed us, saying: Hibban informed us, saying: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: “I was on the day of the battles, and Omar bin Salamah and I were with the women, and I looked, and I was with Al-Zubayr on the His horse would ride to Qurayza two or three times, and when he came back, I said to him: O father, I saw you riding. He said: Or did you see me, oh? My son? I said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who will go to the Banu Qurayza and bring me their news? So I set off. When I returned, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7895","7941 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Abdah bin Sulaiman, he said: I am Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Urwa, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me on the day of Qurayza, and said: May my father be sacrificed for you.” And my mother"
"7896","7942 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: I am Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, saying: I heard Saad bin Malik said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me on the day of Uhud.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7897","7943 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: I am Al-Layth, and Ali bin Khashram informed us, saying: I am Isa, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gathered his parents for me on the day of Uhud. He said: Shoot, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” Qutaibah said: He is fighting, but Qutaibah did not mention: Shoot."
"7898","7944 Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith told us, he said: We are Abu Salih, he said: I am Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Abdullah bin Amer told me, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, first came to Medina, he used to stay up late. night, and he said: I wish a righteous man from among my companions would guard me tonight. While we were like that, we heard the sound of weapons. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Who is this? He said: I am Saad. I came to guard you. She said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept."
"7899","7945 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I am Ismail, he said: I am Qais, he said: I heard Saad bin Malik, saying: “ “I was the first Arab to shoot an arrow in the way of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7900","7946 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Ubaid, he said: I am Sadaqah bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of his grandfather Riyah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid said: “I bear witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Omar is in Paradise, and Othman In Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talha is in Paradise, Al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman bin Awf is in Paradise, and Saad is in Paradise, If I wanted to name the ninth, I would have named him. I am the ninth of the believers, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the tenth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7901","7947 Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: I am Yahya, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad, he said: “It was revealed In me, and in six of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, including Ibn Masoud, they said: O Messenger of God, if you expelled these Those who are insignificant to you are the ones who are indifferent to you. Then it occurred to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and this verse was revealed: And do not expel those They call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening, seeking His face, to His saying: Does not God know best those who are thankful?"
"7902","7948 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, he said: I heard Al-Baraa, He says: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought with a silk garment, and they began to admire its beauty and softness. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “Saad’s handkerchiefs in Paradise are better than this.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7903","7949 Amr bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif narrates, he said: I heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri saying: “The people of Qurayza descended on the rule of Sa’d bin Muadh, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent He greeted Saad bin Muadh, and he came to him on a donkey. When he approached the mosque, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Ansar: Go to your master. Then he said: These people have submitted to your rule. He said: Those who fight against them will be killed, and their descendants will be taken captive. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “I judged according to the judgment of God,” and perhaps he said: “I judged according to the judgment of the King.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7904","7950 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, saying: I am Abu Amir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salih, and Harun bin Abd informed us God, he said: I am Abu Amer, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saleh, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, that Saad ruled Of the Banu Qurayzah, everyone who was subjected to tragedies should be killed, their descendants should be taken captive, and their wealth should be divided. He mentioned That was for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Indeed, the judgment of God has been judged over them, by which God has judged above the seven heavens.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7905","7951 Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, and Yazid bin Abd Allah bin Osama, who is Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace be upon him, greeted Saad while he was being buried: “Indeed, the throne was moved for this righteous servant, and the gates of heaven were opened for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7906","7952 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Yahya, on the authority of Awf, he said: Abu Nadra told me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The throne shook at the death of Saad bin Muadh.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7907","7953 Al-Hasan bin Ahmad told us, he said: Abu Al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : “When it was revealed: And those who accuse chaste women and then do not bring four witnesses, Sa’d bin Ubadah said: O Messenger of God, if I I saw a bag that a man had taken. I would not gather the four until the other had fulfilled his need. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Listen to what he says. \your master\"""""""
"7908","7954 Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: He is Ibn Sulaiman, I am al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik He said: “When it was revealed: O you who have believed, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, and do not speak loudly to him as some of you speak loudly.” For some, your deeds will become futile while you do not realize it. He said: Thabit bin Qais said: By God, I am the one who used to raise my voice before the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I fear that God Almighty became angry with me and became sad and turned yellow, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, lost him. So he asked about him, and it was said: O Prophet of God, he says: I fear that I will be among the people of Hell, for I used to raise my voice before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Rather, he is from the people of Paradise. He said: We used to see him walking between us, a man from People of Paradise\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7909","7955 Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: I am Khalid, he said: I am Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, he said: Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas gave a speech in advance. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Medina, and he said: We prevent you from what we prevent ourselves and our children from, so what is ours? He said: Paradise. He said: \We are satisfied\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7910","7956 Amr ibn Yazid informed us, he said: I am Bahz ibn Asad, he said: I am Shu’bah, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Stolen, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud was mentioned to Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, and he said: “I still love him after I heard the Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Recite the Qur’an four times: He mentioned Abdullah bin Masoud, Salim, the servant of Abu Hudhayfah, and Ubayy. Ibn Ka'b and Muadh Ibn Jabal.\"" 7911"""""
"7911","'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: 'Abdur-Rahman informed us, saying: 'Abdul-'Aziz ibn Abi Hazim informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""What an excellent man is Abu Bakr! What an excellent man is 'Umar! What an excellent man is Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah! What an excellent man is Thabit ibn Qays! What an excellent man is Mu'adh ibn 'Amr ibn al-Jamuh! What an excellent man is Mu'adh ibn Jabal! What an excellent man is Sahl ibn Bayda'."" 'Abdur-Rahman said: Thus did he say, ""Sahl ibn Bayda'."""""
"7912","7958 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ismail, he said: Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, that Umm Harithah came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and Haritha perished on the day of Badr, and was struck by a western arrow. She said: “O Messenger of God, you have known the position of Haritha from my heart. If he was among the people of Paradise, I would not cry over him. Otherwise, you will see what I will do. He said to her: Have you gone foolish? Or is it one Paradise? It is two Paradise Many, and indeed, he is in the highest Paradise.”"
"7913","7959 Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Habban told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sulayman bin al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas He said: “Haritha bin my paternal aunt set out as an overseer on the day of Badr. He set out to fight, but an arrow hit him and killed him. Then my paternal aunt, his mother, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. She said: O Messenger of God, my son Haritha, if he is in Paradise, be patient and seek reward. Otherwise, you will see what I do. So he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Umm Haritha, there are many gardens, and indeed Haritha is in the highest paradise. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7914","7960 Muhammad bin Rafi’ informed us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: I am Muammar, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, He said: It was narrated by Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “I slept and you saw me in Paradise.” So I heard the sound of a woman being recited, so I said: Whose recitation is this? It was said: The recitation of Harithah bin Al-Numan, said the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: Such is righteousness, such is righteousness, such is righteousness, such is righteousness, and he was one of the most kind people to his mother. And the pronunciation is for Ishaq. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7915","7961 Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Ayoub bin Sulayman bin Bilal, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Muhammad, and Musa They said: I am Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I see myself in Paradise. While I was there, I heard the voice of a man reciting the Qur’an, so I said: Who is this? They said: Haritha bin Al-Numan, such is righteousness, such is righteousness. Such is righteousness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7916","7962 Nusayr bin Al-Faraj informed us, he said: I am Shuaib bin Harb, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, he said: I am Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw that I had entered Paradise, and I heard fear in front of me. So I said: Who is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is Bilal, and suddenly there was a white palace in its courtyard, so I said: Who is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is for Omar bin Al-Khattab. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7917","7963 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: I am Abu Usama, he said: Abu Hayyan told me, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Bilal at the dawn prayer: “Tell me about the most promising work that I have done for you in Islam. Yesterday, I heard the softness of your sandals before my hands in Paradise. He said: What I have done in Islam is more disappointing to me than the fact that I did not purify myself completely in an hour. “Night or day, except that I pray to my Lord what is decreed for me to pray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7918","7964 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Ubayd Allah bin Musa, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were six people, and the polytheists said: Drive these people away from you.” They are, and they are. He said: It was me, Ibn Masoud, a man from Hudhayl, Bilal, and two men whose names I have forgotten. He said: So it happened. Meaning within himself what God willed, and he spoke it to himself, then God Almighty revealed: And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening. They desire His face, towards the wrongdoers."
"7919","7965 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala informed us, he said: I am Khaled, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas, saying: The Messenger said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Ubayy bin Ka’b: “Indeed, God Almighty has commanded me to recite the Qur’an to you. He said: He called me fish. He said: Fish. \So he cried\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7920","7966 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he said: Sulaiman bin Amir told us, he said: I heard Al-Rabi’ bin Anas, saying: I recited the Qur’an to Abu Al-Aliya, and Abu Al-Aliya recited to my father, and my father said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “I was commanded to recite the Qur’an to you. He said: Or was I mentioned there? He said: Yes, then my father cried. He said: I do not know whether out of longing or fear. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
